{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through both.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ArraySlice","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass: a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successors.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The components are those of ","type":"text"},{"code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without the trivial ones, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. Empty exactly when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in ","type":"text"},{"code":"attractingComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices do not start at 0.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so one sort by that vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position puts the components in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", where positions are insertion order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(V + E).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"metadata":{"title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Connectivity","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","roleHead